From fbdd9098843bde4e15055befab0780b4798340ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:05:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban annotation: publish one host copy under its
 full inputs; other processes adopt it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Design t_01a1d45d75851804 §2c (review item R9), card t_01a1d471746deeb8. On hermes-hub every web-server
process and the gateway computed the same session-list annotation for the same scope:
`_refresh_annotation_locked` was 13.3% of a steady serve's samples, 10.8% of the gateway's and 12.2% of a
fresh serve's.

- Publish: a refresh takes its inputs before it reads (pinned, so the read keys on exactly them) and writes
  `(scope, fingerprint, read_at, parts)` to `<home>/cache/kanban-annotation/<scope>.host.json` when the read
  answered exactly those inputs (counts cached under that fingerprint and revalidatable). `read_at` is when
  the counts were really read.
- Fingerprint: scope; the boards', hub replica's and sync shadows' content keys (the inputs
  `unchanged_inputs` compares), made portable (a stat key drops its process-local connection; an unreadable
  board or a connection-keyed hub signature means no fingerprint) and required `revalidatable`; the core sha;
  each done check's and waiting source's code identity (core, or its plugin package's file stats when this
  process first saw them); and each waiting source's declared inputs.
- `register_waiting_source(name, fn, inputs=None)`: a source may declare a JSON key that moves whenever it
  could answer differently (e.g. the chat-closeout ledger's revision). When any source declares none, the
  adopter takes the copy's counts but re-runs every waiting source itself, so a source the fingerprint can't
  see is never served from another process.
- Adopt: cold and warm polls that would refresh adopt the copy only on an exact fingerprint and read age
  < `_COUNTS_MAX_AGE_S` (30 s), dated by the copy's own read. Otherwise refresh as before and publish.
- Holder: lease `kanban-annotation` (host_loop_lease); one web-server process per home refreshes every scope
  it can reproduce that any process polled (`<scope>.demand`) in the last 60 s, when the copy is another
  input's or 20 s old. Started next to the annotation prewarm (role serve/dashboard).
- Kill switch `HERMES_ANNOTATION_HOST_COPY=0`.
- The disk copy's encoding now keeps lists and nested dicts (execution evidence), so a decoded copy equals
  the read exactly; older copies still decode.
- `_read_annotation_parts` moves to kanban_annotation_host (kanban_session_activity is at its line cap); the
  name stays bound in kanban_session_activity, so monkeypatches still apply.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_annotation_host.py, 13): adopt on exact fingerprint (no recompute, dated
by the copy); adopted rows == a local refresh (waiting source + done check); declared waiting-source change
defeats adopt; undeclared source re-run by the adopter; stale (>30 s) copy ignored; core sha change and plugin
code change defeat adopt; board write defeats adopt; kill switch; unportable inputs; nested evidence round
trip; holder refreshes a demanded scope once per change.
RED: on the base the new test file fails (module missing). GREEN: the 120 test files importing
kanban_session_activity / kanban_annotation*, 2124 passed.

Follow-up: chat-closeout declares its waiting-source inputs (hermes-mods) so its part is adopted too.
